  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Climate Resilient Communities in Azuero</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The decimation of Panama&apos;s dry forest due to climate change is endangering local species via habitat destruction, and disenfranchising residents as it makes local farmland unusable. This project provides economic opportunities to local communities by granting them micro-contracts to grow saplings that will then be sold and planted to reforest the Azuero Peninsula. Their economic growth will fuel conservation of habitat, biodiversity and create more usable farmland for future generations.</narrative>
  </description>
